{
  "format": "call-of-slop-stations/1",
  // The stations' markets (docs/sandbox/constructs/station.md "Markets"; Karl, 2026-11-18: "The first gameplay loop is being able to dock with
  // it and sell mined ores" and "as a logistics point, it should show up on the friendly market as whatever goods are there to trade").
  // A station is matched by its name (its pieces' section). "power": the NPC power that holds it (Crew/Factions, or a Powers folder): a power
  // hostile to a player doesn't trade with them. There are no credits (Karl, 2026-11-20: barter, option C): what a station pays goes on the seller's tab
  // with its power, spendable only with that power, and what it asks comes off it (Game/GameTabs.cs). Each good: "buy", what the station pays a unit
  // (value on a tab); "sell", what it asks a unit; "stock",
  // what it holds at the start; "most", what it holds at most (it buys no more past that). "margin": the share of what a station pays that its
  // power counts in its stock (the trade it does on it).
  // "haulers" (phase S2; Karl, 2026-11-18: "Haulers from other neutral factions can then send ships to buy goods and take them back to their
  // station"): NPC ships a power runs between two stations, crewed by that power. Each buys "goods" at "from" (what it asks, up to what the
  // ship's bins hold and what the station has), flies there with the Dock order, sells to "to" (what that one pays), loads that station's
  // "back" goods and runs home: the stock moves, and the power's books pay and earn it. "ship" is a blueprint with bins; "count" ships run
  // the route, "wait" seconds moored at each end. A hauler sets out from whichever of its stations is in the world being played
  // (Game/GameStationHaulers.cs); a station's "orbit" (km) is where it meets one at a station in another world.
  // Needs (Karl, 2026-11-20: "we start incorporating needs to the world"): a good's "uses" and "makes" are units an hour of play, taken from and added
  // to its stock (inside 0 and "most") whether its world is being played or not; "want" is the stock it aims for (default half of "most"). Its prices
  // follow the stock: as listed at the want, up to 1.6 times as it runs out, down to 0.6 times at twice the want. A used good under half its want shows
  // SHORT on the card. The Traders (phase 2 of the trade world, docs/sandbox/design/faction-controllers.md "No credits"): Caledon Highport, their hub,
  // burns fuel and steel; Cinder Fuel Depot cracks hydrogen, helium and oxidiser out of Cinder's ground; Slopolis Exchange makes circuits from copper
  // and gold. The Militia's Glacier Watch makes steel from iron ore at the refinery below.
  "margin": 0.25,
  // What things are worth (value, in the old credit prices): a unit of each material, and a part from its Assembling recipe (its materials at these values
  // and the parts in it at theirs) times "work". A part with no recipe is worth "noRecipe". A station's part trades at its value times "partBuy" (what
  // it pays) and "partSell" (what it asks) unless the station's own row says "buy" or "sell". A material not listed is worth 0.5.
  "values": {
    "work": 1.25, "noRecipe": 2, "partBuy": 0.8, "partSell": 1.25,
    "dirt": 0.01, "stone": 0.03, "sand": 0.03, "wood": 0.1, "planks": 0.2, "concrete": 0.1,
    "iron ore": 0.15, "copper ore": 0.25, "gold ore": 1.1, "levite ore": 2,
    "metal": 0.65, "steel": 1.2, "copper": 0.8, "gold": 3, "bronze": 1, "levite": 6,
    "glass": 0.3, "rubber": 0.4, "cloth": 0.3, "laminate": 0.6, "circuits": 3.75,
    "hydrogen": 0.4, "helium": 0.6, "oxidiser": 0.4, "ammo": 1.8
  },
  // The Traders' first supply lines (phase 2; the ships are placeholders until Karl's Traders ships are in: change "ship" to swap one in).
  // Convoys (phase 3): "needs": true also loads any good the far station is short of that this one sells, most needed first (a listed good
  // the far one is full of stays behind). "escort" puts "count" (up to 4) warships of the power with each hauler, holding "gap" m beside it
  // (three times that off a station while it docks); the hauler waits up to two minutes past its "wait" for them before a leg. A lost escort
  // is replaced at the hauler's next station a minute on. The Traders' Zero Day is the placeholder escort.
  "haulers": [
    { "power": "Traders", "ship": "Magpie Mining Ship", "count": 1, "from": "Caledon Highport", "to": "Glacier Watch", "goods": ["iron ore", "copper ore"], "back": ["steel"], "wait": 30, "needs": true,
      "escort": { "ship": "Zero Day Frigate", "count": 1, "gap": 150 } },
    { "power": "Traders", "ship": "Magpie Mining Ship", "count": 1, "from": "Cinder Fuel Depot", "to": "Caledon Highport", "goods": ["hydrogen", "helium"], "back": ["metal"], "wait": 30, "needs": true,
      "escort": { "ship": "Zero Day Frigate", "count": 1, "gap": 150 } },
    { "power": "Traders", "ship": "Magpie Mining Ship", "count": 1, "from": "Caledon Highport", "to": "Slopolis Exchange", "goods": ["copper ore", "gold ore"], "back": ["circuits"], "wait": 30, "needs": true,
      "escort": { "ship": "Zero Day Frigate", "count": 1, "gap": 150 } },
    // Hexkey Orbital's supply (Karl, 2026-11-21): furniture from the flat-pack works at Slopolis Exchange, in the ship's Storage Volumes, by what
    // the store is short of ("parts": true), in the Packet Spine Freighter's standard containers (Karl, 2026-11-21: the new Traders ship as the placeholder).
    { "power": "Traders", "ship": "Packet Spine Freighter", "count": 1, "from": "Slopolis Exchange", "to": "Hexkey Orbital", "goods": [], "back": [], "wait": 30, "parts": true,
      "escort": { "ship": "Zero Day Frigate", "count": 1, "gap": 150 } }
  ],
